{
  "case_id": "2007-06-939",
  "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In AB 1889, California defunded employer speech about union organizing because the State's labor policy is that such speech interferes with employee free choice. The Federal policy is that employer speech enhances employee free choice. California's labor policy is designed to discourage exactly what the NLRA promotes. The fact that California implemented its labor policy as an exercise of its spending authority is irrelevant under Gould. If the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about the spending clause question? You -- the Federal Government has a lot of programs where they use their own money and they come with a lot of conditions, and you -- your office frequently argues that those are justified under the spending clause. Why isn't what California is doing here similarly justified?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hungar",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State does not have any obligation under the Act to fund unionization speech, but what it can't do under the Act is deny a government benefit because of a -- a labor policy. That's what this Court held in Nash."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hungar",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was labor policy. I mean, you have to acknowledge it was labor policy in these other cases, just a different labor policy that the Federal Government wanted, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am I correct in assuming that if the State of California had its labor relations agency make it an unfair labor practice to engage in this employer speech described here, that that would be pre-empted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GOTTESMAN",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position, however, is that it's quite different to say that the National Labor Relations Act requires the State to pay for these activities. And --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: That's what I'm asking."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GOTTESMAN",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, you've got for or against. This is content discrimination, not viewpoint discrimination; and it is content discrimination whose purpose is to keep the State's funds out of this area of context. The taxpayers' money should not be spent supporting one side and not the other in these disputes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I think your reason for not paying for this activity is that you don't like this activity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GOTTESMAN",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This court in the Linn case -- and I want to quote this sentence, because this is the key to why a policy of neutrality with respect to the use of the State's money is not, you know, regulated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GOTTESMAN",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the Ninth Circuit thought erroneously is that Boston Harbor had denied it the right to take that same view, because it thought that Boston Harbor said that everything is regulation unless it's market participation, and that's not what Boston Harbor said, and this is not regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldsmith",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0003-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The State has no business making labor policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about the Lyng case that Mr. Gottesman cited in response to that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "California",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California has taken it much farther than simply withdrawing the subsidy. California has taken it to the point that you're exposed to treble damages, but then you have minute tracking and segregation of fund details, and California has taken it even one step farther and said on the other hand, if you want to spend State money to facilitate union organizing, that's perfectly fine with us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-939",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "ef7a6fd9aebf9087690e9a9f8fdc3f277a6ee9a4fc595115ef060b31ec332e62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef7a6fd9aebf-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
